Samong brand assets — NOT covered by Apache-2.0
===============================================

Copyright 2026 Samong contributors. All rights reserved.

The files in this directory — samong-mark.svg, samong-mark-mono.svg,
samong-wordmark.svg, samong-wordmark-mono.svg, samong-lockup.svg,
samong-lockup-mono.svg — and the name "Samong" are **excluded from the
Apache-2.0 licence that covers the rest of this repository**.

This file exists because the exclusion needs to be where the files are. The
repository's root LICENSE is Apache-2.0, which grants broad rights to copy and
redistribute; Apache-2.0 section 6 withholds trademark rights but says nothing
about artwork as a copyrighted work. Someone cloning this repository has no
reason to guess that these six files are different unless it is stated here.


What you may do without asking
------------------------------

Use these marks to refer to Samong: writing about it, linking to it, a
screenshot, a talk slide, a "works with Samong" badge on your own tool,
packaging Samong for a distribution. This is nominative use and it is welcome.

Keep the shapes and proportions as published, and follow the usage rules in
site/brand.html: the clear space, the minimum size, exactly one lit node, and no
outlines, shadows, gradients, rotation, stretching or re-spacing of the letters.
Recolour only by using a -mono file, which draws in currentColor.


What you may not do
-------------------

Use these marks, or the name "Samong", as the identity of your own product or
service, or on a fork you distribute under a different name. Fork the code
freely — Apache-2.0 means it — but ship it under your own name and your own
mark. A user who sees this logo should be able to conclude they are looking at
Samong.

Do not register these marks, or anything confusingly similar, as a trademark.


Fonts
-----

The wordmark files contain outlined letterforms extracted from Bai Jamjuree
(Cadson Demak), which is licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The OFL
governs redistribution of *font software*; outlined artwork is not font
software, and the font itself is not modified or redistributed here. Licence
copies for every bundled font are in site/fonts/.

Nothing in this file restricts your rights to the font under the OFL.


Asking
------

For anything not covered above, open an issue at
https://github.com/waanvar/samong.
